problem:
Problem description
- There is a planning horizon made up of periods $$t \in \mathcal{T}$$, with the given instance corresponding to a weekly production setting.
- There is a set of liquid products $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$; the instance contains the product categories corresponding to $$A$$ and $$B$$.
- Each product has a unit profit $$\pi_p$$, a unit production-time requirement $$\tau_p$$, and a unit storage-space requirement $$\sigma_p$$.
- The planning goal is to choose nonnegative production quantities so that total profit from all sold output is maximized.
- The total production time used in any period must not exceed the available production capacity $$H_t$$.
- Market-mix requirements may impose minimum proportional output relationships between selected products, represented by ratios $$\rho_{pq}$$.
- Storage usage is limited through the product-specific storage coefficients and any direct storage cap parameters $$U_p$$.
- The business rules require that the output of product $$B$$ must be at least a fixed multiple of the output of product $$A$$.
- The business rules require that product $$A$$ uses more storage space per unit than product $$B$$.
- The business rules also impose a direct upper bound on the amount of product $$A$$ that can be stored in the period.
- All decision quantities must remain nonnegative.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_{p,t}$$: the quantity of product $$p$$ produced or sold in period $$t$$.
  - $$z$$: the total profit achieved by the plan.

Input Format
{
  "time_horizon": {
    "periods": "array of period identifiers with length $$|\mathcal{T}|$$",
    "unit": "planning period label, such as weekly"
  },
  "products": {
    "product_ids": "array of product identifiers with length $$|\mathcal{P}|$$"
  },
  "parameters": {
    "unit_profit": "vector $$\pi_p$$ for $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$",
    "production_time_per_unit": "vector $$\tau_p$$ for $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$",
    "storage_space_per_unit": "vector $$\sigma_p$$ for $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$",
    "available_production_time": "vector $$H_t$$ for $$t \in \mathcal{T}$$",
    "minimum_mix_requirements": "list of records $$\langle p,q,\rho_{pq} \rangle$$ meaning product $$p$$ must be produced in at least $$\rho_{pq}$$ times the quantity of product $$q$$",
    "direct_storage_caps": "optional vector $$U_p$$ for $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$ giving any direct upper bound on stored quantity"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "production_plan": {
    "quantities": "array or table of records $$\langle t,p,x_{p,t} \rangle$$ with shape $$|\mathcal{T}| \times |\mathcal{P}|$$"
  },
  "objective_value": "scalar $$z$$ representing total profit"
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "time_horizon": {
    "periods": ["week_1"],
    "unit": "weekly"
  },
  "products": {
    "product_ids": ["A", "B"]
  },
  "parameters": {
    "unit_profit": {
      "A": 30,
      "B": 10
    },
    "production_time_per_unit": {
      "A": 6,
      "B": 3
    },
    "storage_space_per_unit": {
      "A": 4,
      "B": 1
    },
    "available_production_time": {
      "week_1": 40
    },
    "minimum_mix_requirements": [
      {
        "product": "B",
        "reference_product": "A",
        "minimum_multiple": 3
      }
    ],
    "direct_storage_caps": {
      "A": 4
    }
  }
}
